# scripts/* (not scripts/) so a single script can be re-included below:
# git cannot un-ignore a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded.
scripts/*
config/

# The simulator screenshot + click-test harness is source-controlled — the
# broker's simshots mode runs it from a fresh clone.
!scripts/simulator-screenshots.sh
# Its capture configuration has to travel with it. The broker clones fresh, so
# an untracked config file would simply not exist on the runner and the capture
# would silently fall back to the default text size — the one configuration in
# which the Dynamic Type overflow is invisible. Deliberately NOT named *.env:
# that pattern is for secrets, and this file must be readable in the clone.
!scripts/simshots-config.sh
!scripts/simshots-pick-device.py
!scripts/simshots-export-attachments.py
!scripts/imagegen/
!scripts/imagegen/**

# The local test database is the difference between a functional test and a
# test that cannot log in. Without it /api/auth/signin answers 503, Playwright
# never gets past sign-in, and /upload renders its signed-out shell with no file
# input — a state that looks identical whether the upload feature works or not.
!scripts/dev-testdb.sh

# ShotIQ product specifications and automated tests are source-controlled.
!basketball-analysis/docs/
!basketball-analysis/docs/superpowers/
!basketball-analysis/docs/superpowers/**
!basketball-analysis/tests/
!basketball-analysis/tests/**

# Large files
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
!basketball-analysis/public/**/*.png
!basketball-analysis/public/**/*.jpg
!basketball-analysis/src/**/*.png
!basketball-analysis/src/**/*.jpg
# The canonical design sets are the SPEC for the 1:1 fidelity work — every
# measurement is taken against them. A container rollback already destroyed the
# scratchpad copy once. They live in git so that cannot happen again.
!basketball-analysis/docs/shotiq/canonical/*.png
!basketball-analysis/docs/shotiq/canonical-desktop/*.png
# The iOS asset catalog is the app's shipping artwork, not an incidental image.
# Without this, `git add -A` silently skips a new imageset's PNG while happily
# committing its Contents.json, so the build gets an asset entry pointing at a
# file that is not there and the screen falls back to its placeholder. That is
# exactly what happened to the two recent-capture thumbnails on 026: the commit
# said the photos were cut and shipped, and the next capture still showed two
# black rectangles. The existing 003/004 PNGs were force-added by hand, which
# is why the trap was invisible until someone added a third.
!basketball-analysis/ios-native/**/Assets.xcassets/**/*.png

